# Money & IDs

## Decimal — Never Float

All monetary and quantity values use `github.com/shopspring/decimal`. Never use `float32` or `float64` for financial values.

```go
// ❌ BAD
price := 0.1 + 0.2  // float precision error

// ✅ GOOD
price := decimal.NewFromString("0.1")
total := price.Mul(qty)
```

- Serialise to DB as `NUMERIC` — never `FLOAT`
- Serialise to JSON as a quoted string to avoid precision loss: `"0.10000"`
- `Amount` on every `LedgerEntry` must be **strictly positive** (`d.IsPositive()`)

## Double-Entry Invariant

For any completed `Transaction`, across each `AssetID`:
```
sum(credits) == sum(debits)
```
Validate this in the AR before calling `Complete()`.

## IDs — Always kernel.ID

All domain identifiers use `kernel.ID` (a typed wrapper over `uuid.UUID`).

```go
// ❌ BAD
userID string
userID uuid.UUID

// ✅ GOOD
userID kernel.ID
```

- Generate new IDs with `kernel.NewID()`
- `IdempotencyKey` fields are `string` but must be non-empty — validate at construction
